# ledger-mcp

An [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server for the Ledger API. It wraps the
[`ledger`](https://pypi.org/project/ledger/) Python SDK and exposes one tool per
API method, named `<resource>_<method>`:

- `customers_list`: List customers, newest first
- `customers_create`: Create a customer
- `customers_search`: Search customers by name
- `customers_get`: Fetch one customer
- `customers_update`: Change a customer's name, email or metadata
- `customers_delete`: Delete a customer and all their unpaid invoices
- `invoices_list`: List invoices
- `invoices_create`: Create a draft invoice
- `invoices_get`: Fetch one invoice
- `invoices_finalize`: Turn a draft invoice into an open one and email it to the customer
- `invoices_void`: Void an open invoice so it can no longer be paid
- `invoices_download_pdf`: Download the invoice as a PDF
- `payments_list`: List payments
- `payments_get`: Fetch one payment
- `refunds_create`: Refund all or part of a payment
- `files_upload`: Upload a file, such as a receipt, as a multipart form
- `files_upload_raw`: Upload a file as the raw request body
- `events_stream`: Stream account events as they happen

## Install

```sh
pip install ledger-mcp
```

Requires Python 3.10 or newer.

## Run

The server speaks MCP over stdio.

```sh
ledger-mcp
```

Example client configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "ledger": {
      "command": "ledger-mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

Tool results are JSON. Binary responses are written to the directory in
`LEDGER_MCP_OUTPUT_DIR` (a temporary directory by default) and the tool returns the file's path
and size. Set `LEDGER_BASE_URL` to point the server at a different API host.
